/-!
# Equivariant families of coefficient endomorphisms: pointwise application to data, adjointness and Shapiro coordinates

Formalized by Claude Sonnet 5.5.

An equivariant family `P : Fam W Z` of `ℚ`-linear endomorphisms of `W`, indexed by labels, acts pointwise on cochains of the model resolution (`Fam.act`), on line and plane data (`LineDatum.act`,
`PlaneDatum.act`) and on cone cochains.  The cone pairing is adjoint for pointwise adjoint families (`conePair_lineCone_act`, `conePair_planeCone_act`), the Shapiro coordinate of an acted datum is the image of
the coordinate under the value of the family at the representative (`LineDatum.act_coord`), and the family generated by a map commuting with the stabilizer of a label is `famOfStab`.
-/

